<!--
    Issue #862, SPARC V9 (64-bit): the same dropped call result as
    kuna-sparc-callreturn.xml.  SparcV9_64.cspec now kills o0, fd0 and fd2
    (its output registers) at every call.

        f1:  atoi(a0); a0 = (int4)a0 + 1; return a0;
        fd:  dd(); *a2 = a0;

    Stage: P4 calls and prototypes (call output trials).  No option.
    Source (clang 14 -fintegrated-as -fno-pic, sparcv9-linux-gnu; the calls
    are relocated to undefined stubs at 0x80000+), -O2 at 0x10000 and -O0
    (names suffixed _O0) at 0x20000:
        int f1(const char *s) { return atoi(s) + 1; }
        char *f2(const char *s) { char *p = getenv(s); return p ? p + 1 : 0; }
        int f3(const char *a, const char *b) { int x = atoi(a); int y = atoi(b); return x - y; }
        void fd(double x, double *p) { *p = dd(x); }
    Asserts #1-#5: each call's result is used where the code uses it.
    Assert #6: no call prints as a bare statement with its result dropped.
-->
